---
title: Skål
template: quiet
---
Skål exists because double-clicking a Markdown file on a Mac gets you either a wall of punctuation or an invitation to set up a workspace. Skål opens the file as a document. Read it rendered in Live, work on the exact source in Code, or keep both in view in Split. Open and save without touching anything and the file comes back byte for byte; make an edit and only the lines you changed change.

No account, no library, no new format. It's still just the `.md` file you had, and Finder can now preview it before you open anything at all.
